<title>FRANCE: Dehaene &quot;understands&quot; French EMU budget pact stand.</title>
<headline>Dehaene &quot;understands&quot; French EMU budget pact stand.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian Prime Minister Jean-Luc Dehaene said in a French newspaper interview published on Monday his country understood France's position on the EU &quot;stability pact&quot; and said the pact itself should not be called into question.</p>
<p>&quot;I understand the French moves because Belgium has the same approach,&quot; Dehaene told business daily Les Echos. &quot;We already called for an employment chapter in the Maastricht treaty a year ago but found little support,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>&quot;What is also important is that no one calls the stability pact in itself into question,&quot; he was quoted as saying.</p>
<p>It was not clear what day the interview took place. The Les Echos newspaper does not have weekend editions.</p>
</text>
